<title>SINGAPORE: FCC full year net profit up nine pct.</title>
<headline>FCC full year net profit up nine pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    122.16 vs 112.0</p>
<p>Dividend (cents)			14.0 vs  12.0</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     49.1 vs  49.6</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)   41.2 vs  40.4</p>
<p>    Turnover				609.07 vs 465.82</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   16.45 vs  7.11</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		3.11 vs  1.29</p>
<p>    Losses from associates		8.29 vs  1.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			211.50 vs  177.39</p>
<p>    Tax					78.88 vs  53.87</p>
<p>    Minorities		    9.05 (loss)  vs  10.46(loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    47.02 (gain)  vs   5.21(gain)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: December 5</p>
<p>Last day books open: to be advised  </p>
<p>Note - FCC said it expected to do well in the current financial year. The extraordinary item came mainly from the sale of investments by associated companies.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199</p>
</text>
